sections.body:
`else` provides the alternative - no condition needed:

```python
if temp > 25:
    print("Warm")
else:
    print("Not warm")
```

When there are several cases, `elif` ("else if") checks conditions in order and stops at the first true one:

```python
if temp > 30:
    print("Hot")
elif temp > 20:
    print("Pleasant")
elif temp > 10:
    print("Cool")
else:
    print("Cold")
```

Exactly ONE branch runs. Once a condition matches, the rest are skipped. Order matters: put the most specific checks first.

example.code:
score = 78

if score >= 90:
    print("Grade: A")
elif score >= 80:
    print("Grade: B")
elif score >= 70:
    print("Grade: C")
else:
    print("Keep practising!")

passed = score >= 60
if passed:
    print("You passed the quiz.")

